            "description": "Status Quo (2022) and projection (2030) of biomass capacities aggregated for transmission grid in Germany for the EOM-Plus project.                     2022 data based on freely available data (e.g.  Marktstammdatenregister (MaStR), tendering results, Renewable Energy Sources Act (EEG) annual statements).                     Biomass plants divided into five categories: BGP_FF2=Biogas CHP not very flexible (with storage restriction),                     BGP_FF4=Biogas CHP very flexible (with storage restriction), BM=Biomass CHP plant (mainly wood) (without storage restriction),                      BME_ALT=Biomethane CHP existing (without storage restriction), BME_NEU=Biomethane CHP new construction (without storage restriction).                     Installed capacity = maximum active electrical capacity; rated capacity = balance of the kilowatt hours actually produced within                     a calendar year divided by the sum of the full hours in the year, corresponds to the constant inflow into the biogas storage facility;                     biogas storage capacity = maximum equivalent amount of electricity that can be stored in the biogas storage facility.                     2030 projections via linear interpolation of scenario B in NEP37/45 and tender volumes according to the EEG for biomass and biomethane                     until 2028. The development of the biomass stock is based on the assumption that currently very inflexible biogas CHP plants and                     biomass CHP plants < 10 MWel will shut down by 2030. The regionalization of new construction for biomethane from 2023 is assumed to be                     evenly distributed across all transmission grid nodes within the southern region defined under the EEG. The aggregation is based on                     the allocation of the municipal areas of all facilities to the nearest transmission network node.",
